# Genesis seal switch
#
# Changing this file triggers .github/workflows/genesis-seal.yml, which runs three dumps to
# the private Storage bucket, in order:
#
#   1. site + ops   from AIP2            — the nightly backup, run for real once
#   2. cfb          from AIP2            — the weekly backup, run for real once
#   3. every schema from the OLD project — public, study, docs, voice, cfb: the seal
#
# All three are reads, so none of them is affected by database write state. (For the record:
# AIP2 went briefly read-only right after the cfb restore, under platform disk-pressure
# protection, and came back on its own about five minutes later when the disk auto-grew.)
#
# Robert's pause click on the old project comes AFTER leg 3 verifies. Do not pause first:
# the dump is the thing that makes the pause safe.

run: 5
requested-by: clyde
reason: >-
  genesis Job 4, fifth attempt. Run 4 fixed the DDL check (242 DDL lines, 92 tables, parse
  exit 0 on a 380 MiB cfb dump) and then hit a real platform limit rather than a bug:
  the upload returned 413 EntityTooLarge. A Supabase project has a GLOBAL upload ceiling
  separate from the per-bucket file_size_limit — the bucket allows 50 GB and 380 MB was
  still refused. Raising it is a dashboard setting, so backup.sh now splits anything above
  the ceiling into parts with a manifest carrying the whole dump's sha256, which makes the
  backups independent of that setting entirely.
